WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.590 --> 00:00:05.020
Shazam's 21st century adventure on the big
screen is an origin story, so don't worry

00:00:05.020 --> 00:00:06.840
too much if you're going in cold.

00:00:07.140 --> 00:00:09.720
Just make sure you're paying attention and
enjoy the ride.

00:00:09.940 --> 00:00:14.040
But even if you aren't familiar with the characters,
you're certainly going to see a few familiar

00:00:14.040 --> 00:00:15.720
faces bringing them to life.

00:00:15.980 --> 00:00:18.420
Here's why the cast of Shazam! looks so familiar.

00:00:18.600 --> 00:00:21.660
Oh, and just in case you haven't seen the
movie yet?

00:00:21.660 --> 00:00:22.660
Spoilers ahead.

00:00:23.580 --> 00:00:28.480
Seeing as he's playing the supersized version
of young Billy Batson otherwise known as Shazam

00:00:28.480 --> 00:00:33.480
Zachary Levi is essentially the face of the
film, and probably the most recognizable face

00:00:33.480 --> 00:00:34.180
all around.

00:00:34.480 --> 00:00:36.760
"I'd like to purchase some of your finest
beer, please."

00:00:41.360 --> 00:00:46.040
With any luck, Shazam! will give the supremely
talented Levi that final push onto the Hollywood

00:00:46.040 --> 00:00:46.740
A-list.

00:00:46.960 --> 00:00:48.380
Wondering where you've seen him before?

00:00:48.640 --> 00:00:51.740
Well, Shazam! is hardly Levi's first superhero
flick.

00:00:52.100 --> 00:00:57.190
The actor last suited up for cosmic action
as Fandral alongside his fellow Warriors Three

00:00:57.190 --> 00:00:59.600
in Thor: The Dark World and Thor: Ragnarok.

00:00:59.820 --> 00:01:04.620
It's far more likely that you recognize Levi
from his extensive work on the small screen.

00:01:04.920 --> 00:01:09.939
Most recently, he appeared in the short-lived
series Heroes Reborn, and starred in the cheeky

00:01:09.940 --> 00:01:11.770
NBC sitcom Telenovela.

00:01:12.340 --> 00:01:18.000
He also impressed with a serious turn in Netflix's
marvelous dramatic mini-series Alias Grace.

00:01:18.260 --> 00:01:23.259
Of course, Levi is probably best known for
his work on NBC's awesome, oft-overlooked

00:01:23.260 --> 00:01:24.660
action/dramedy Chuck.

00:01:25.170 --> 00:01:29.380
The actor brought some serious geek energy
to his charming portrayal of a directionless

00:01:29.400 --> 00:01:34.360
post-grad who inadvertently downloads a secretive
government computer program into his brain.

00:01:34.580 --> 00:01:37.160
And yes, it's every bit as fun as it looks.

00:01:38.160 --> 00:01:42.600
Shazam! could also prove the first big break
for the actor portraying Billy Batson, the

00:01:42.600 --> 00:01:44.660
pint-sized version of Levi's superhero.

00:01:45.420 --> 00:01:46.200
"Are you for real?"

00:01:46.420 --> 00:01:46.920
"Say it!"

00:01:46.920 --> 00:01:47.420
"Okay!"

00:01:47.520 --> 00:01:51.780
We're guessing that most of you don't know
who Asher Angel is, because he's just getting

00:01:51.780 --> 00:01:53.140
started in showbiz.

00:01:53.540 --> 00:01:57.450
Some of you may recognize the youngster from
his one-off role in the short-lived spin-off

00:01:57.450 --> 00:01:59.640
series Criminal Minds: Beyond Borders.

00:01:59.900 --> 00:02:04.779
A few of you might also have even seen Angel
as the second lead in the 2018 ballet drama

00:02:04.780 --> 00:02:05.959
Driven to Dance.

00:02:06.380 --> 00:02:11.260
If not, those of you with the Disney Channel
might just recognize Angel as the conspicuously

00:02:11.260 --> 00:02:15.260
kind-hearted Jonah Beck from the family-friendly
comedy Andi Mack.

00:02:15.640 --> 00:02:19.170
Whether you're familiar with Angel's work
yet or not, we're fairly confident you'll

00:02:19.170 --> 00:02:23.800
be seeing his face a lot moving forward possibly
even in a Shazam! sequel!

00:02:25.060 --> 00:02:29.620
The actor playing his precocious, crutch-bound
best pal Freddie Freeman has been on the Hollywood

00:02:29.620 --> 00:02:31.380
radar for few years now.

00:02:31.960 --> 00:02:33.320
"Dude, just messing around.

00:02:33.540 --> 00:02:35.040
You look at me and you're like, 'Why so dark?

00:02:35.049 --> 00:02:36.049
You're a disabled foster kid.

00:02:36.049 --> 00:02:36.700
You've got it all!"

00:02:37.100 --> 00:02:43.120
His name is Jack Dylan Grazer, and he got
his first taste of stardom with a brief appearance

00:02:43.120 --> 00:02:45.510
in 2015's chilling horror anthology Tales
of Halloween.

00:02:45.780 --> 00:02:50.280
He followed that family-friendly outing with
a starring role in the TV series Me, Myself

00:02:50.280 --> 00:02:55.380
and I, a comedy exploring key moments in a
man's life over three distinct time periods,

00:02:55.640 --> 00:02:58.420
with Grazer portraying the youngest version
of the protagonist.

00:02:58.720 --> 00:03:03.019
The up-and-coming actor went from relative
unknown to impressive newcomer when he joined

00:03:03.019 --> 00:03:07.879
the Losers Club as the nervous, overprotected
Eddie Kaspbrak in the brilliant adaptation

00:03:07.880 --> 00:03:13.660
of Stephen King's It — a role Grazer is
ready to reprise in 2019's hotly-anticipated

00:03:13.660 --> 00:03:14.160
sequel.

00:03:14.360 --> 00:03:18.500
In between those horrifying blockbusters,
Grazer also booked the prime gig of playing

00:03:18.500 --> 00:03:22.860
the adolescent version of Timothee Chalamet's
character in the indie hit Beautiful Boy.

00:03:23.880 --> 00:03:27.180
Grace Fulton is likely to be familiar to quite
a few viewers.

00:03:27.340 --> 00:03:31.980
Fulton portrays Billy and Freddie's foster
sister Mary Bromfield in Shazam!, and much

00:03:31.999 --> 00:03:36.840
like her co-star Jack Dylan Grazer in It,
Fulton has likewise played the younger version

00:03:36.840 --> 00:03:38.040
of a character in a film.

00:03:38.260 --> 00:03:42.760
In fact, one of Fulton's biggest early roles
came as the adolescent version of ill-fated

00:03:42.760 --> 00:03:48.140
Hollywood starlet Natalie Wood in the 2004
TV movie The Mystery of Natalie Wood.

00:03:48.500 --> 00:03:52.560
She followed that role with a recurring gig
as the younger version of Jennifer Love Hewitt's

00:03:52.560 --> 00:03:54.799
Melinda Gordon in The Ghost Whisperer.

00:03:54.880 --> 00:03:59.760
Later, she booked a multi-episode gig as the
teenage counterpart to Madeleine Stowe's matriarch

00:03:59.760 --> 00:04:01.420
on ABC's Revenge.

00:04:01.780 --> 00:04:06.450
Of course, most viewers will recognize Fulton
as one the eldest of the tormented orphans

00:04:06.450 --> 00:04:11.340
in 2017's chilling addition to the Conjuring
universe, Annabelle: Creation.

00:04:12.380 --> 00:04:17.180
Shazam! finds Djimon Hounsou playing an ancient
wizard who gives Billy Batson the power to

00:04:17.180 --> 00:04:18.300
transform into Shazam.

00:04:18.709 --> 00:04:23.160
Hounsou spent the early years of his career
as a fashion model and backup dancer in music

00:04:23.160 --> 00:04:26.800
videos for Tina Turner and Janet Jackson,
among many others.

00:04:27.000 --> 00:04:31.280
Steven Spielberg used his own wizardry to
pull a heartrending breakout performance from

00:04:31.280 --> 00:04:34.160
the model-turned-actor in 1997's Amistad.

00:04:34.600 --> 00:04:39.540
The film made an overnight star out of Hounsou,
who has gone on to appear in dozens of films,

00:04:39.540 --> 00:04:44.310
including memorable turns in Ridley Scott's'
Gladiator, the heartrending 2002 drama In

00:04:44.310 --> 00:04:50.870
America, and the fast-paced 2015 action film
Furious 7, even earning a few Oscar nominations

00:04:50.870 --> 00:04:51.840
in the process.

00:04:52.220 --> 00:04:56.560
If you're wondering where you've seen Hounsou
recently, it was likely in the MCU, where

00:04:56.560 --> 00:05:01.240
the actor portrayed the Kree warrior Korath
in both Guardians of the Galaxy and Captain

00:05:01.240 --> 00:05:01.740
Marvel.

00:05:02.560 --> 00:05:07.200
Speaking of Shazam! actors who have superhero
experience, let's not forget about the great

00:05:07.200 --> 00:05:08.220
Mark Strong.

00:05:08.440 --> 00:05:14.150
The iron-jawed actor plays the nefarious Dr.
Thaddeus Sivana in this latest DC flick, but

00:05:14.150 --> 00:05:17.080
Shazam! is far from Strong's first turn as
a super-baddie.

00:05:17.320 --> 00:05:22.020
He actually played another DC villain almost
a decade ago in that oh-so-forgettable Ryan

00:05:22.020 --> 00:05:23.720
Reynolds-starring Green Lantern.

00:05:23.840 --> 00:05:27.820
Of course, Strong may just have a face for
villainy, because he broke bad again as the

00:05:27.820 --> 00:05:31.080
vile Frank D'Amico in 2010's Kick-Ass.

00:05:31.340 --> 00:05:36.200
Strong also played memorable villains in the
big screen adaptation of Neil Gaiman's Stardust.

00:05:38.640 --> 00:05:41.160
“ahhh”

00:05:44.220 --> 00:05:49.180
And try not to forget the 2009, Robert Downey
Jr.-starring Sherlock Holmes, where he played

00:05:49.180 --> 00:05:50.780
the evil Lord Blackwood.

00:05:50.980 --> 00:05:54.199
Did you happen to catch his performance in
Ridley Scott's Robin Hood, where he played

00:05:54.200 --> 00:05:54.700
Godfrey?

00:05:54.880 --> 00:05:59.820
Rest assured, the role of the bad guy in Shazam!
is in the hands of an extremely good actor.

00:06:00.200 --> 00:06:04.680
He's also starred in the Kingsman movies,
the 2008 thriller Body of Lies, Zero Dark

00:06:04.760 --> 00:06:06.660
Thirty, and countless other films.

00:06:07.660 --> 00:06:11.900
The actor playing the adult version of Freddy
Freeman will likely need no introduction.

00:06:12.120 --> 00:06:16.500
Adam Brody did, after all, get his first big
break with a multi-episode stint as would-be

00:06:16.500 --> 00:06:18.720
rocker Dave in Gilmore Girls.

00:06:18.900 --> 00:06:23.560
His follow-up role as the ever-nerdy Seth
Cohen on The O.C. helped the young actor achieve

00:06:23.560 --> 00:06:25.500
full-on teen heartthrob status.

00:06:26.000 --> 00:06:28.060
"I'm sorry if I'm the only one here who will
state the obvious."

00:06:28.060 --> 00:06:28.560
"Seth—"

00:06:28.580 --> 00:06:30.180
"but we have all this extra room, right?

00:06:30.180 --> 00:06:31.140
We have a pool house."

00:06:31.140 --> 00:06:36.080
Brody has also made scene-stealing appearances
in movies like the 2014 coming of age drama

00:06:36.090 --> 00:06:42.110
Growing Up And Other Lies, Wes Craven's meta-horror
sequel Scream 4, and Whit Stillman's Damsels

00:06:42.110 --> 00:06:43.080
in Distress.

00:06:43.129 --> 00:06:47.740
Dyed-in-wool horror fans will most likely
recognize Brody for his disturbing and hilarious

00:06:47.740 --> 00:06:52.740
turn as an indie-rocker with some serious
ulterior motives in the bloody Diablo Cody

00:06:52.740 --> 00:06:54.260
satire Jennifer's Body.

00:06:55.140 --> 00:06:59.980
Freddie Freeman isn't the only one of Shazam's
pint-sized pals to get a superhero alter ego

00:06:59.980 --> 00:07:00.580
in the movie.

00:07:00.800 --> 00:07:05.120
In fact, most of Billy's foster fam earn spots
in the super-powered "Shazam Family."

00:07:05.500 --> 00:07:09.800
The inimitable Meagan Good scored the role
of the adult Darla Dudley, who undergoes a

00:07:09.800 --> 00:07:12.780
truly radical transformation throughout the
course of the film.

00:07:13.270 --> 00:07:16.260
If you're wondering where you've seen her
before, take your pick, 'cause she's been

00:07:16.260 --> 00:07:20.740
cranking out movies on the regular since breaking
into showbiz in the mid-'90s.

00:07:20.860 --> 00:07:25.680
Of her work in that bygone decade, most will
recognize Good as the confused big sis in

00:07:25.680 --> 00:07:27.740
the coming-of-age drama Eve's Bayou.

00:07:28.400 --> 00:07:33.440
In the years since, Good has racked up memorable
roles in TV shows like Californication, and

00:07:33.440 --> 00:07:36.140
the sadly short-lived Minority Report series.

00:07:36.280 --> 00:07:40.700
She's also nursed a booming big screen career
that's seen her appear in films like Anchorman

00:07:40.700 --> 00:07:45.800
2: The Legend Continues and the entirely unfortunate
2008 comedy The Love Guru.

00:07:46.080 --> 00:07:51.820
"And now, I'd like to show my love by making
for you the Quebec pizza."

00:07:52.240 --> 00:07:52.780
"What's that?"

00:07:53.240 --> 00:07:54.580
"Pop Tart with the ketchup."

00:07:55.080 --> 00:07:59.740
And don't forget you bloodcurdling work in
the horrific and outright horrible Saw 5.

00:08:00.060 --> 00:08:02.960
Here's hoping Shazam! helps make a household
name of Good.

00:08:03.860 --> 00:08:08.140
Of the actors playing adult, super-powered
versions of younger characters in Shazam!,

00:08:08.150 --> 00:08:10.870
Michelle Borth isn't one of the better-known
names.

00:08:10.870 --> 00:08:15.199
Still, that doesn't mean you won't recognize
the face of the future Mary Marvel or Lady

00:08:15.200 --> 00:08:19.220
Shazam or just plain ole Mary, AKA Mary Bromfield.

00:08:19.550 --> 00:08:23.220
Though Borth has yet to find a legitimate
breakthrough role in Hollywood, she's been

00:08:23.220 --> 00:08:25.180
in the game for a couple of decades now.

00:08:25.490 --> 00:08:29.520
Hawk-eyed viewers might recognize Borth for
a one-off appearance as Dean's significant

00:08:29.520 --> 00:08:31.860
other in a trippy episode of Supernatural.

00:08:32.260 --> 00:08:35.960
Or perhaps you caught her in HBO's relationship
drama Tell Me You Love Me.

00:08:36.140 --> 00:08:41.680
Odds are most of you know Borth from her 60-episode
run as Catherine Rollins on Hawaii Five-O.

00:08:41.840 --> 00:08:45.720
And if you don't know Michelle Borth from
any of those projects, now's as good a time

00:08:45.720 --> 00:08:49.160
as any to learn her name, because you'll be
hearing it for years to come.

00:08:49.960 --> 00:08:54.380
Just a few years ago, most viewers would not
have been able to pick actor Ross Butler out

00:08:54.380 --> 00:08:59.920
of a lineup even if his 6'2" frame unquestionably
set him apart from most of his peers.

00:09:00.160 --> 00:09:04.290
While viewers still may not have Butler's
name memorized, it's a safe bet they'll recognize

00:09:04.290 --> 00:09:09.160
his face from one of several notable small
screen appearances over the past few years.

00:09:09.420 --> 00:09:14.600
The actor first started turning heads in 2015
when he appeared in Disney Channel's action

00:09:14.600 --> 00:09:15.340
comedy K.C.

00:09:15.340 --> 00:09:15.840
Undercover.

00:09:15.860 --> 00:09:20.580
That same year, Butler booked one of his highest-profile
gigs when he claimed the role of tough-guy

00:09:20.580 --> 00:09:23.980
jock Reggie Mantle in The CW's surprise hit
Riverdale.

00:09:24.500 --> 00:09:29.010
With an obvious penchant for teen drama, Butler
again played a tough-guy jock with a conscience

00:09:29.010 --> 00:09:32.480
in Netflix's teen suicide drama 13 Reasons
Why.

00:09:32.720 --> 00:09:37.320
Though he's yet to find his breakout role,
Ross Butler is very much a star on the rise,

00:09:37.320 --> 00:09:41.530
and there's little doubt that his work as
the superpowered adult version of Eugene Choi

00:09:41.530 --> 00:09:43.470
will set his star a little bit higher.

00:09:44.540 --> 00:09:49.400
The actor playing the father of Shazam! baddie
Dr. Sivana will need no introduction to fans

00:09:49.400 --> 00:09:53.190
of the superhero genre the DC Universe in
particular.

00:09:53.190 --> 00:09:58.020
The actor's name is John Glover, known for
his giddily wicked work as Lionel Luther on

00:09:58.020 --> 00:10:00.960
the long-running "Superman in high school"
drama Smallville.

00:10:01.420 --> 00:10:05.190
In addition to his voice work as the Riddler
in Batman: The Animated Series, fans of the

00:10:05.190 --> 00:10:10.120
Dark Knight should also recall Glover's face
for his appearance as the mad scientist Dr.

00:10:10.120 --> 00:10:13.440
Jason Woodrue in 1997's Batman &amp; Robin.

00:10:13.940 --> 00:10:18.960
Love it or hate it, Glover's maniacally over-the-top
performance was unquestionably one of the

00:10:18.960 --> 00:10:21.940
best parts of Joel Schumacher's controversial
farce.

00:10:22.220 --> 00:10:26.660
If you managed to miss Glover in those super-powered
flicks, you'll probably still recognize his

00:10:26.660 --> 00:10:27.160
face.

00:10:27.500 --> 00:10:31.720
He's a beloved character actor who's been
working steadily in showbiz since the '70s.

00:10:32.080 --> 00:10:36.660
Among Glover's more memorable roles are appearances
in the Oscar-winning dramedy Annie Hall.

00:10:37.160 --> 00:10:38.180
"You know how I'd like to die?"

00:10:38.180 --> 00:10:39.180
"No, how?"

00:10:39.760 --> 00:10:42.560
"I'd like to be torn apart by wild animals."

00:10:42.620 --> 00:10:48.290
And let's not forget his stupendously scene-stealing
work opposite Bill Murray in 1988's Scrooged.

00:10:48.340 --> 00:10:53.960
Oh, and then there was his equally delicious
role in the 1990 sci-fi sequel, RoboCop 2.

00:10:59.600 --> 00:11:00.400
"Magno-volt!

00:11:01.180 --> 00:11:02.660
The final word in auto security."

00:11:03.060 --> 00:11:07.480
That's to say nothing of his memorably hilarious
turn as the head of the Clamp Cable Network

00:11:07.480 --> 00:11:10.280
in the cult classic Gremlins 2: The New Batch.

00:11:10.480 --> 00:11:14.880
There's plenty of other roles worth mentioning,
like his part in John Carpenter's unheralded

00:11:14.880 --> 00:11:17.080
masterpiece In the Mouth of Madness.

00:11:17.260 --> 00:11:20.920
All we really want to say about John Glover
is that he's one of those actors who makes

00:11:20.920 --> 00:11:23.420
us smile the second he turns up on screen.

00:11:23.820 --> 00:11:25.880
Check out one of our newest videos right here.

00:11:26.040 --> 00:11:29.420
Plus, even more exclusive Looper videos about
your favorite films are coming soon.

00:11:29.900 --> 00:11:33.340
Subscribe to our YouTube channel and hit the
bell so you don't miss a single one.

